        mid_desc2:
          "Hazarchishma Natural Bridge is located 100 km north of Band-e-Amir National Park at the northern edge ofBamyan Province, near the border with Samangan Province. The arch is a young meander natural bridge carvedthrough limestone karst in Jawzari Canyon (Dara-i-Jawzari), which joins the Ajar valley as part of the AmuDarya watershed and the main Caspian basin. In the recent geological past, the river became subterranean,leaving Dara-i-Jawzari dry. The elevation of the arch is 3100 meters (10,000 feet) above sea level. It alsoranks among the largest such structures known.",
